# Full playthrough, title screen to the sportsman ending (see README.md).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --minigame-stub=jardim --ms 660000 --input tools/play/full.input [--dump DIR]
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --minigame-stub=jardim --ms 660000 --fix all,-avi_exit_ignores_timer --input tools/play/full.input
#
# The run is deterministic (headless virtual clock): the random choices
# (roadblock cop, hall doors, TIRO's targets, ENCAIXE's pieces, bar quiz question) depend
# on the time of the calls, so changing the timing of an earlier line can
# change them. With the fixes, leave out the two that change the route
# (README.md):
#   --fix all,-avi_exit_ignores_timer
# The hall's TIRO, the pharaoh's ENCAIXE and the gym's SALGIN are the real
# minigames (scripted wins, tools/tiro_plan.py, tools/encaixe_plan.py and a
# held Up for SALGIN); with `--minigame-stub` the run fails at their
# `result` lines. The street's XILINDRO runs too, unplayed (B21, below).
# The garden's JARDIM at the end stays the stub (`--minigame-stub=jardim`),
# which wins: JARDIM is tested by its own scripts (jardim-*.input).

# Title menu: JOGAR, then NOVO JOGO; the opening video ends in the bedroom.
22000 dump title
